The Allow Notifications button was missing before because unconfigured server VAPID keys caused the app to hide the button behind a static notice, and the card inside Notifications was placed below the filter tabs. That is now fixed so the Allow Notifications button is always shown and triggers the device permission prompt whenever you are signed in and notifications have not yet been allowed or blocked.
Where to find it (when signed in)
Top of Notifications: Tap Alerts in the bottom bar on mobile (or the bell icon at the top right on desktop) — the Allow device notifications card with the Allow Notifications button now appears right below the Notifications header.
Main Feed Banner: A dismissible Allow device notifications banner appears at the top of the feed until you allow, block, or dismiss it.
Mobile Menu Drawer: Tap the 3-line menu icon (☰) at the top right — Allow Notifications appears right under the app install control.
Account Settings: Open Settings → Privacy & Visibility under Push Notifications & App Install.
Android vs. iPhone differences
Android (Chrome / Edge / installed app): Works immediately in both the browser and the installed app as long as you are signed in.
iPhone / iPad (iOS 16.4+): Apple blocks notifications in regular Safari tabs, so Safari shows an Add to Home Screen card first; once you add LASUED Intel to your Home Screen and open it from the Home Screen app icon while signed in, the Allow Notifications button appears in all the places above. (Note: if you open the preview inside an embedded frame or while signed out, sign in and open the site directly in its own browser/app window, and remember background closed-app push still requires setting your Firebase VAPID keys in Vercel.)
Checkpoint
Browser Notifications Allowed — Awaiting Server Push Keys
Real-time in-app alerts are active. Background Web Push notifications when the app is closed will finish activating automatically once VAPID keys and Firebase Admin credentials are configured.
